# Standing UI (CalFresh dashboard)

Add new visual preferences here **and** as a standing rule in `TODO.md` plus a bullet under README “Frontend Implementation Notes,” so later views don’t re-litigate them.

## Hover values

- Disable Chart.js canvas tooltips (`tooltip.enabled: false`).
- Render values in the HTML `.chart-hover` box via `hoverTooltipExternal(..., 'above')`.
- Follow the hovered month on x. Sit **entirely above the canvas** (title/caption band), never on the lines, stacks, or bars. County bar charts use `'above'` too — not beside-the-caret. Use `position: fixed` so the outcomes grid’s `overflow-x` and row titles cannot clip the box. On Participation, keep the box below the sticky shared-controls bar (`stickyControlsFloor`); hover `z-index` is 30 vs the bar’s 20.
- Caseload movement hover lists bands top-to-bottom as drawn (ICT in, Reinstated, Other approvals, Approved, Discontinuances, Net). The Other approvals rescinded note is a footer under the rows, not above them.
- Nested volume strips stay inside their own `.received-plot` so they don’t cover the mix chart above. All-application received (Master_Monthly `Applications Received`) lives on the **Total applications** row. College student stacks use `New Applications Age Total` (not CF296 Item 1). SSI stacks use `Online Apps - SSI` + `Non-Online Apps - SSI` (not the SSI-only online/non-online pair, and not CF296 Item 1). Nested mix titles use the same metric-then-place stack as Outcomes (short row name, then muted population · place).
- When a mix share uses a starred 1–10 cell plotted as 5, prefix hover percents with `~` and put this footer under the rows: “Some data has been masked for this report month; %s are estimates.” Do not interpolate through months with two or more large hidden cells; still draw a complete month that sits between those gaps (`isolatedStackSlices`).
- Stacked mix hover includes the count those percents are of: **Applications disposed** (all), **College student applications disposed** — not `New Applications Age Total` — **SSI household applications disposed**. Student mix hover also notes applications still pended, which are not in the mix. Channels hover is Applications received (all / SSI) or the student source total. Denial details hover is applications denied. Age / Language / Race / Gender hover is the matching student Age/Language/Race/Gender total, SSI households disposed (language), or SSI persons in applications disposed (race). Household size hover is SSI-only households added, plus SSI average age. Exemptions & deductions hover is student age total or SSI household applications disposed; rates do not sum to 100%. Student Age hover includes average age; student volume hover notes ICT transfers; SSI volume hover includes average age. # mode on those rows uses the same denom as a count, with a unit footer. Timeliness hover is Applications disposed (after 30 days) or Expedited applications found entitled (after 3 days); each row includes that count. Days to process hover is initial applications approved (CF18; Expedited / Non-expedited listed under the overall when one place is shown) or SSI household applications disposed. Churn hover is **households scheduled** named by the selected clock — Combined **Of N households scheduled for a recertification or SAR 7 report**, Recertification **…for recertification**, SAR 7 **…for a SAR 7 report** — **applications disposed** (Who applied), or **reapplications** (Reapplication Outcomes and Time to reapply). Time to reapply hover is sentences: of N reapplications, X% (count) came back that month; then eligible vs ineligible of that month — not “Share of reapplications” plus nested Eligible (churn). Snapshot due-chart hover lists the five bands only — no nested timely / untimely / lag splits (those live in the reapplication fold-outs). The hover note names the selected Combined / Recertification / SAR 7 clock. Who applied nests restoration and 1 vs 2–4 months prior (approved vs denied) under Recent SAR 7 Due and Recent Recert Due. Recertification / SAR 7 Outcomes by County hover is the five bands plus households scheduled — no nested timely / untimely / lag splits. Both county lineups also trail the California Sort-by rate and the group’s combined Sort-by rate (the same bands as the dashed California and group lines). Item 7 average days of lost benefits is in the **Estimated Lost Benefits** fold-out under the due chart (and still a hover footer), not a band. That fold-out is closed by default, with a combined total of late with loss plus eligible reapplications.

## Channels

- All applications and college students share **GetCalFresh**, **BenefitsCal / Other Online**, and **Other**. SSI uses the same last two names plus **GetCalFresh (SSA)**.
- All applications: GetCalFresh = `All_GCF_apps_submit`, BenefitsCal / Other Online = `Online Applications Received` − GetCalFresh, Other = `Applications Received` − Online. After June 2025 GetCalFresh is 0; dashed marker at July 2025. Do not mix student sources with `CfA_GCF_apps_submit`.
- Students: GetCalFresh = `Applications Submitted via Code for America`, BenefitsCal / Other Online = Other Online Source + BenefitsCal, Other = Other Source.
- SSI: **GetCalFresh (SSA)** = `SSA_GCF_apps_submit` (SSA office filings via GetCalFresh on behalf of SSI recipients). BenefitsCal / Other Online = `Online Apps - SSI` − GetCalFresh (SSA). Other = `Non-Online Apps - SSI`. Last nonzero SSA GCF is September 2024; after that GetCalFresh (SSA) is 0. If SSA GCF exceeds Online SSI, leave the month blank — CalWIN counties often reported 0 SSI online/non-online December 2019–May 2022 while SSA GCF was still filled.

## Layout

- Application Outcomes grid rows expand from full-width section labels (Outcomes open by default; Total applications / Channels / Age / Language / Race / Gender / Household size / Exemptions & deductions / Denial details start closed). Age, Language, Race, Gender, and Household size are who-applied mixes (not outcomes by group), with a per-row **# / %** toggle (default %). Exemptions & deductions are overlapping **rates** (not a 100% stack) with the same toggle. Do not use a left-hand label column — it steals plot width — or a Break out checklist under the grid.
- A **What are procedural denials?** call-out sits at the bottom of Application Trends (after the mix, always open — not a fold). Definition plus a 1% impact estimate for the selected place and the last month of the date range. Compare Populations lists All / college student / SSI; Compare Places uses the selected population. Same teal estimate-callout treatment as Churn’s Estimated Lost Benefits.
- Date range and place filters (Counties / Regions / County size) live **on Application Trends**. Matching date and place values stay in sync if more than one control is on that section. Do not use a sticky page-level bar on this view. Snapshot / county-bar charts keep their own independent lists (empty = all counties). **Timeliness** follows Application Trends date and place (no separate bar). Participation Trends uses a sticky `#sharedControls` bar for **Total Participants and Annual % Change only**. The bar unsticks at **Annual % Change by County** (that chart keeps its own lists). Leave space between that chart’s county filter toggle and the plot title, same buffer as under the compact date/place bars. **When folded**, that bar and **Caseload movement**’s date/place bar are a compact summary of the date range and place with **Expand to change what you see** — not the date-range slider. Slider, presets, and geography lists appear only when expanded. Caseload filters start matching the top bar until the user changes them. Both **% Change in CalFresh Participants** and **% Change by County** use a **Show Quarterly Change** / **Show Annual Change** button in the title row (Diana, 2026-09-09). The two charts keep their own setting. Quarterly is persons vs three months earlier, not a calendar-quarter average.
- Application Outcomes Compare **Places / Populations** lives on Application Trends. Compare **Populations** shows only **County** in Application Trends filters (hide Regions, County size, and Drill). Clicking a county replaces the current place and stays in Populations. Places mode keeps the full lists.
- Stacked mix charts label bands on the canvas (`stackBandLabels`). Skip HTML color legends above those plots. The procedural slice is **Procedurally Denied**, not Procedural (parallel with Approved / Withdrawn / Denied). The county line-up group-aggregate stays **Procedural**. Student Denial details ungroups the large reason types; Other is the tiny remainder.
- Plot titles (and captions in the same `.chart-plot`) start at the left edge of the data area, not over the y-axis ticks. `--plot-title-inset` is set from Chart.js `chartArea.left` (`plotTitleAlign`).
- Application Outcomes mix titles stack **metric then place** (All applications / Sacramento), not `County — Title`. That keeps every column’s header the same height so the plots line up. Place is the smaller muted line under the metric. Nested plots (Total applications / Channels / Age / Language / Race / Gender / Household size / Exemptions & deductions / Denial details) use the same two-line stack: short row name, then muted **population · place** so a screenshot or a scroll past Outcomes still names the column.
- Application Outcomes section order: Application Trends, then the county snapshot, then **Timeliness**, then Sources. Timeliness is **Applications** (default) or **Recertifications**. Applications: CF296 **After 30 days** and **After 3 days (expedited)** overlay on **Processed late**, plus **Average Days to Process** (CF18 / Quarterly, SSI from Monthly) **side by side** (stack under 800px), plus a closed **How long did approvals take?** fold-out. Recertifications: Item 10 ÷ Item 9 overdue rate; hide ES 3-day and CF18 days; current-era Item 9.a.1 overdue-day buckets on the right. **Caseload movement** is last on **Participation Trends**, after Annual % Change by County and before Sources. Do not overlay it on Total Participants. It has its own date/place bar on the card (not the sticky `#sharedControls` bar). Those filters start matching the top two charts until the user changes them. Do not auto-add California from Add Statewide comparison.
- **Churn** (`churn.html`): **What is Churn?** first (lay explainer: what it is, why it matters, the two measurements), then two California section cards (latest complete CF18 month; no **California snapshot** title), then two stacked county lineups, then Sources. **Recertification / SAR 7 Outcomes** and **Applicants’ Prior CalFresh Connection** each have Month and County pickers at the top; the two stay in sync. Month also drives both county lineups. County defaults to California (in the list) and does not filter the county lineups. Subtitles: “Churners” are those that reapply, shown in orange; “Churners” are those with recent recertification or SAR 7 due, shown in purple. Explainer names jump to those headings. Recertification / SAR 7 Outcomes includes Combined / Recertification / SAR 7 / Side by side plus Reapplication Outcomes / Time to reapply / Estimated Lost Benefits fold-outs. Applicants’ Prior CalFresh Connection is Who applied. Default **Combined** is one stacked chart, **Recertification & SAR 7 Outcomes**, summing Recertification and SAR 7 counts (a household is on one clock or the other). **Show Combined / Recertification / SAR 7 / Side by side** — Combined, Recertification, and SAR 7 each show one chart; Side by side is the two clocks (stack under ~800px). Fold-outs follow (Outcomes open; Time and Lost benefits closed). **Reapplications** is one orange band on top of each stack (Items 9–16). Those two stacks use on-canvas **value** labels, with leader lines for thin bands and always for Reapplications. Applicants’ Prior CalFresh Connection (Who applied) uses the same on-canvas value labels. Who applied hover nests restoration and 1 vs 2–4 months prior (approved vs denied), not later. **Reapplication Outcomes** and **Time to reapply** are Application-style fold-outs under the due stacks (Outcomes open; Time closed). Same Recert | SAR 7 columns. Outcomes is Eligible / Ineligible of Items 9–16. Time to reapply is **when they came back** (four bars: Next month / 2 / 3 / 4 months; **# / %** toggle, default % of those reapplications, bars sum to 100%). Time hover is plain language (of N reapplications, X% (count) came back that month; then eligible vs ineligible of that month). Reapplication Outcomes is the eligible / ineligible mix. An **Estimated Lost Benefits** fold-out (closed by default) follows Time to reapply (combined total of late with loss plus eligible reapplications; Item 7 average days lost plus estimated dollars). The Show Combined / Recertification / SAR 7 / Side by side toggle updates the combined total (Side by side still uses the Recert + SAR 7 total). Who applied that month is Measurement 2 with its own plum/olive palette. Two county lineups follow the snapshot cards: **Recertification / SAR 7 Outcomes by County** (same Recertification / SAR 7 stack; Sort by No loss, No return, or Reapplications, default no loss; Combined / Recert / SAR 7 report type, default Combined; Group by county size) and **Applicants’ Prior CalFresh Connection by County** (Who applied stack; Sort by Recent Recert & SAR 7 Due (sum of those two bands), Other Recently On, or New, default Recent Recert & SAR 7 Due). Each has its own Group by and filters. Leave a little space between the county filter toggle and the plot title. Grouped like Participation’s Annual % Change by County, dashed California combined-rate line on the sorted band. Group labels are a short Sort-by name plus rounded % on a white chip with a Sort-by band-colored border; hover trails the California Sort-by rate and that group’s combined Sort-by rate. No sticky page-level bar. No Compare populations. No time-series stacks as the primary view. Mix titles stack metric then place. On-canvas band labels; skip HTML color legends. Short explainer copy lives in **What is Churn?**; the two section cards get a one-line churner subtitle, not a second explainer. Days to approval stays on Applications.
- Timeliness (Diana, 2026-09-04; days 2026-09-04; one percent chart 2026-09-04; side-by-side / days colors / SSI toggle 2026-09-04; Applications | Recertifications 2026-09-09): **Show Applications / Recertifications** on the Timeliness card. Applications (default): **After 30 days** and **After 3 days (expedited)** overlay on one chart (`tension: 0`), plus **Average Days to Process**. A closed fold-out **How long did approvals take?** is two 100% stacks of CF18 expedited / non-expedited approval-count buckets; hover is of N approvals, X% (count) in that band. Recertifications: Processed late is CF296 Item 10 overdue (county-caused) ÷ Item 9 disposed — hide the expedited 3-day line. CF18 days are initial applications only, so hide Average Days / SSI and show current-era Item 9.a.1 overdue-day buckets instead (legacy has none). Percents are CF296 only — no student/SSI timeliness cells. Hover includes the count each percent is of. Days to process uses CF18 (weighted) preferring that over the Quarterly tab’s `Average Days to Approve`. SSI days are Monthly `Average Days to Dispose - SSI`. Follows Application Trends date/place. Days palette is purple all-apps `#5B4B8A` / terracotta SSI `#C17B5C`. Not a county ranking bar.
- Total Participants layers (Diana, 2026-09-09; SNB/TNB one toggle 2026-09-09; title/caption 2026-09-09): **CFAP** (California only, default off) sits with SNB / TNB in the layer list, not at the top. Checking it restacks All Participants into federal SNAP (bottom `#FB7906`) + CFAP (top `#2C5985`) — same height as the umbrella total, not extra people. Uncheck All Participants to read the CFAP band on its own scale. Do not label CFAP as “state-only.” **SNB / TNB** is one stacked toggle (SNB bottom `#6B3D5A`, already in the total; TNB top `#C17B5C`, extra, not on CF 256). **$ Issued** follows visible person layers: All on → Total Issuances; All off + CFAP on → state-funded issuances (CFAP), including mixed-household CFAP slice; SNB/TNB on add those EBT dollars (excluded from Total Issuances). **Unemployment rate** (EDD, not seasonally adjusted) shares the right axis with $ Issued — checking one turns the other off. Axes from 0. Simple definitions notes sit under the layer list when those layers are on, and in footer Definitions / Data notes / Wonky details. Caption lists the checked layers (checkbox order) after the place. Title stays **Total CalFresh Participants** while All Participants is on, or when overlays are locked. Uncheck All, one person layer: **CalFresh Participants by Age Group**, **CalFresh College Students**, **CalFresh Participants Also Enrolled In Medi-Cal**, **CalFresh Participants in Child-Only Households**, **CFAP Participants**, **SNB / TNB Participants**. Several person layers: **CalFresh Participants**. $ Issued / unemployment do not steal that title. CFAP restack caption says **Federal SNAP and CFAP**, not extra people. All off + CFAP $ Issued caption is **State-funded issuances (CFAP)**. Multi-place captions stay “monthly persons” (layers locked).
- Quality Control (`qc.html`, Diana, 2026-09-09; explainer 2026-09-09): overlay **Active Error Rate** and **Negative Error Rate**. Default California. Hover on negative includes completed-cases n. Cumulative FFY; 19 PMC counties own rates, 39 others pooled. No ranking bar. Rates lag; empty months are gaps. An always-open **What these rates mean** call-out (same teal treatment as procedural denials) sits under the section title: Active = households already getting CalFresh, wrong amount; Negative = denials and closings, that “no” was wrong. Neither is a fraud rate; the two percents are not comparable.

## Axes and color

- Every vertical axis starts at zero (`min: 0`, or `beginAtZero: true` if the series can go negative).
- Caseload movement: left (stacks) and right (net) share min/max (`movementScaleExtents`). Hide the right-axis tick labels; Net still uses a hidden `y1` so it is not stacked with additions/exits. Hover and the accessible table still show net with a `+` via `fmtNet`.
- Caseload movement uses each CF296 Part C figure **in the month it was reported** (Diana, 2026-09-03; same-month 2026-09-03). Adds: Item 5.a Applications approved, Item 5.e **Other approvals** (typically rescinded discontinuances — they offset prior-month Item 7, they are not shifted onto that prior month), Item 5.d reinstated prorated, and Item 5.c **ICT in** (incoming only). Discontinuances are the **full Item 7** count, including ICT outs — CF296 has no ICT-out cell. Statewide, ICT in and those outs should cancel in the net. Item 5.b is omitted (Total is 0). Do not subtract Item 9.b recert ineligible from Item 7 (it can over-count). Chart band is **Other approvals** (report name). Hover lists bands top-to-bottom as drawn; the rescinded note is a footer under the values. Stack bottom→top: Approved `#4BA5BA`, Other approvals `#2E6F62`, Reinstated `#6BA3C4`, ICT in `#8B9AAB` (cool grey), Discontinuances `#FB7906` (negative, fill to origin). `tension: 0`.
- Application outcomes colors (brand, same meaning on every mix): approved `#4BA5BA` (teal), denied procedural `#FB7906` (orange), denied ineligible `#6A6A6A` (muted grey). Withdrawn `#C0C0C0`, pended `#C4D6E4`. Lumped Denied — student headline Denied, and SSI months with no ineligible/procedural split — is `#A89890` (warm grey), never the procedural orange. That is what made SSI “spikes” look like a procedural surge when the month was only Approved + Denied. Stacked 100% mixes use `tension: 0` so a one-month lumped Denied does not cubic-overshoot into neighboring months. Fill each band to the previous slice (`stackFill`), not origin — origin fills paint every SSI extra layer over Approved and grey the teal.
- Application outcomes (all applications, CF296): stack bottom→top: approved, withdrawn, ineligible, procedural.
- Application outcomes (college students, Master_Monthly): share of applications disposed (approved + denied). Pended is still in process — hover only, not in the mix. When the nine denial-reason columns are close to denied, stack bottom→top: approved, denied (lumped months only), other, ineligible, procedural — same shape as SSI. Otherwise Approved + Denied of those two columns (early 2023). Ineligible groups ineligible + ineligible CF student + over income; Procedurally Denied = procedural + missed interview + FTP income + failed determination. Denial details ungroups the six large types. Procedural-denial sort is available in this mode.
- Application outcomes (SSI households, Master_Monthly): when ineligible + procedural is close to denied, 4-way Approved / Ineligible / Procedurally Denied / Other. Otherwise Approved + Denied of that two-part total (CalWIN ~2020–May 2022). Stack bottom→top: approved, denied (lumped months only), other, ineligible, procedural. Unused slices are 0 and omitted from hover. Do not blank months that have approved and denied.
- County-bar group-aggregate lines are dashed. Participation uses dark grey `#555` (bars are not grey). Application Outcomes uses black `#111` so the line stays visible across withdrawn (`#C0C0C0`) and ineligible (`#6A6A6A`) stack segments. On Application Outcomes, show the line that matches **Sort by** (approval vs procedural denial) — not both at once. Left-align the on-canvas label at the start of the group; put the approval label **below** the line (on the blue) and the procedural label **above** the line (on the orange). The county line-up aggregate stays **Procedural** (short); stacked mixes keep **Procedurally Denied**. Churn county lineup labels are a short Sort-by name plus rounded % on a white chip with a Sort-by band-colored border, left-aligned at the group start; hover also lists that group rate.
- Average Days to Process uses its own palette so it does not read as another Processed late view: all-applications purple `#5B4B8A` (`DAYS_ALL_COLORS`), SSI terracotta `#C17B5C` (`DAYS_SSI_COLORS`). SSI county lines are dashed. Do not reuse `COMPARE_COLORS` on that chart.
- Churn due-chart colors (Diana, 2026-09-04; CA snapshot 2026-09-04; combined Reapplications 2026-09-07; lost-benefits total 2026-09-07; combined due chart 2026-09-07; due hover bands-only 2026-09-07; county hover bands-only 2026-09-08; due hover clock note 2026-09-09; who values / prior hover 2026-09-09; county combined / no-loss default 2026-09-09): stack bottom→top **No loss of benefits** `#2C5985`, **Late with loss** `#4BA5BA`, **Ineligible** `#6A6A6A`, **No renewal and no return within 4 months** `#C0C0C0`, **Reapplications** `#FB7906` (top). Orange `#FB7906` on this page is a new application after a missed recert/SAR 7 (Measurement 1 only) — not procedural denial, and not reused on Who applied. Reapplication Outcomes uses Eligible `#FB7906` and Ineligible `#F4A261`. Time to reapply uses Reapplications orange `#FB7906`. Who applied (Measurement 2) uses a forest / olive / wine / rose family: **New / not recently on** `#3D6B4F`, **Other Recently On** `#8A9A6B`, **Recent SAR 7 Due** `#6B3D5A`, **Recent Recert Due** `#A56B7D`.

## Defaults

- Default **Compare populations**, California. Places is the other mode (counties, regions, or size groups side by side for one population). California stays in the Counties list; selecting it there is how you compare to the state. Participation Trends defaults to California (Add Statewide comparison is disabled while California is already selected; it still adds a dashed reference when a county or region is chosen instead). Churn defaults to **California**, latest complete CF18 month.
- Default date range: last 24 months.
- Consortia is obsolete; size buckets are XL / L / M / S.
- Do not impute 5 on a starred Part C **Total** or on applications-received — those stars are often complementary large cells. Recover Part C as PACF + NACF; only use 5 for a starred PACF or NACF **part** when Total is also missing. Small-cell `*` treatment lives in `data.js`. Same rule on Churn: do not impute 5 on a starred CF18 Item 1 (households scheduled) or Item 17 (applications disposed).

## Drill-down

- **Drill into group** is enabled when exactly one region **or** exactly one county size group is selected (not 0, not 2+ of the same type). Clicking it sets Counties to that group’s member counties and leaves the grouping selected so its aggregate (or size filter) stays on the chart. Do not stuff California/Statewide into Counties — Participation uses Add Statewide comparison for that. If both one region and one size are selected, Counties follows the **region** (members still limited by the size filter). Put the recipe in the drill `.info-tip`, not a caption.

