- Optional Notice quirk break (Diana, 2026-09-03): a small doodle in the far corner of the header row (opposite the DJ lockup — not the Notice Scout badge, not a floating button, not in the nav). Hover/focus: **“Distract me with something quirky!”** Click opens **Animals with Appropriate Accessories** (arrows through the set; no image titles on the overlay). Esc / backdrop / close returns to the same charts. It must not compete with charts, sticky `#sharedControls`, or chart hover (`z-index` 50 for the overlay vs hover 30 / bar 20). Hide it in print. Shared `quirk.css` / `quirk.js` / `assets/quirk/`.

## Copy

- Keep on-page captions and chart titles short. Put recipes, small-cell `*` treatment, source column names, and cannot-overlay caveats in `.info-tip` bubbles, footer Data notes, and the collapsed **Wonky & math-y details** fold (after Data notes). Not in paragraphs above the charts — except Churn’s **What is Churn?** section, Application Trends’ **What are procedural denials?** call-out (definition plus the 1% impact sentence), and Quality Control’s **What these rates mean** call-out. Color/clock reading notes stay in Data notes, not in that explainer.
- Caseload movement’s section `.info-tip` is **Net is additions minus discontinuances.** Same-month / Other approvals / ICT recipes stay in Data notes and Wonky details — do not put them back in the i-tip.
- Timeliness’s section `.info-tip` is **Share decided after the 30-day or 3-day deadline, plus average days to process. Higher is later. Lines overlay.** CF296 / CF18 / Quarterly recipes stay in Data notes and Wonky details.
- Churn snapshot i-tip covers the two clocks. **What is Churn?** covers the lay definition and the two views: **Recertification / SAR 7 Outcomes** shows churning cases as a share of cases with certain reports due in a specific month; **Applicants’ Prior CalFresh Connection** shows churning cases as a proportion of all application processing work. Those names are the two section titles (and jump links from the explainer). Plot captions name the selected report month (**Of households scheduled for recertification (RRR) or a SAR 7 in January 2026** / **Of households scheduled for recertification (RRR) in January 2026** / **Of households scheduled for a SAR 7 in January 2026** / **Of CalFresh and CFAP applications disposed in January 2026.**). Grey vs orange ineligible, two-clock caveat, and CalSAWS note stay in Data notes and Wonky details. Snapshot due-chart hover is bands only; the hover note names the selected clock (Combined: Of N households scheduled for a recertification or SAR 7 report). Recertification / SAR 7 Outcomes by County hover is bands only too, and trails the California Sort-by rate plus the group’s combined Sort-by rate.
- User-facing copy says **CDSS Data Dashboard Monthly tab**, not `Master_Monthly`. That is the Monthly sheet in the Excel file on the CDSS dashboard page. Keep `Master_Monthly` in code and internal docs.
- Do not name the back-end sheet (**CalFresh Data - Consolidated**) on the page. The live-note is “Data sources last refreshed DATE.” Named sources stay in the footer. After each linked county report (CF296, CF18), a parenthetical links the current ACL that tells counties how to complete it — e.g. CF296 (ACL 22-85), CF18 (ACL 18-117). Not on the CalFresh Data Dashboard link.
